    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751-a1">

                <pb facs="0911" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg817"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Senate resolution, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-05">December 5, 1895</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">imprisonment of general
                        sanguily</hi>.</p>
                <p>Mr. Call submitted the following resolution; which was considered by unanimous
                    consent, and agreed to:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That the Secretary of State be directed to
                    send to the Senate all correspondence relating to the trial, conviction, and
                    sentence to hard labor for life of <pb facs="0912" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/>
                    General Sanguily, an American citizen, for alleged complicity in the war against
                    Spain by the Cubans, and if no authentic record should be on tile in the State
                    Department, that the Secretary of State be directed to obtain a copy of the
                    record of such trial.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
